There's a similar system in Omega (another roguelike) in which you have
to carefully organise your bag to avoid rummaging around for ages when
a nasty approaches. It seemed like an excellent game, but I found that
particular inventory system quite annoying to use; to the extent that I
pretty much gave up on it after about an hour.

With very careful planning, this could be an interesting feature, but I
feel that it would be such a drastic departure from the current system
that it wouldn't be NetHack anymore. Not only that, but it'll make the
resultant game even _more_ difficult - I find vanilla hard enough as it
is, and I've been playing for years (though the bad habits certainly
don't help).

Maybe this would be better suited to those players that have many
ascensions under their belts and are looking for a new challenge. Or
newer players that aren't yet set in their ways. ;o)



